// TEST: LeafIdx over a malformed degree sequence (rejects)
// The derived axes share TreeIdx's bad-shape channel, deliberately: a malformed
// sequence is the same mistake whichever former named it, so LeafIdx plants the
// same marker record and surfaces as the same BL4021 with the same text.
//
// The sharing is what makes the registerTypeDecl carve-out necessary. LeafIdx
// aliases take the ORDINARY nominative path (the alias name becomes the tag),
// and without an explicit exemption for the error marker that overwrite would
// drop the error kind and the smuggled detail, turning this file's BL4021 into
// a plain index alias over a placeholder extent.
// REJECT-AT: lower
type BadLeaf = LeafIdx<[2, 0]>
let L: Array<Float64 like BadLeaf> = [1.0, 2.0]
// ERROR: BL4021
// ERROR-CONTAINS: truncated degree sequence
